## Summary

String-VR content (TEXT, ST, UT, LO, SH, PN, ...) nested inside a Sequence (SQ) element is decoded using a hard-coded `TextDecoder("latin1")` instead of the decoder derived from the dataset's `SpecificCharacterSet` (0008,0005), even when that attribute correctly declares e.g. `ISO_IR 192` (UTF-8) and appears before the sequence in the dataset. Top-level (non-nested) string attributes in the *same file* decode correctly. The corruption is on the **read** side only — the bytes written for non-ASCII content are correct UTF-8.

Observed on dcmjs 0.50.1 (`dcmjs.data.DicomMessage`/`DicomMetaDictionary`), but the relevant code appears unchanged on `master` as of this writing.

